  "summary": "QpiAI has unveiled India's most powerful quantum computer, the 25-qubit Indus Quantum Computer, marking a significant milestone in the country's quantum computing capabilities. The company has outlined plans for future systems with increased qubit counts, including 64, 128, and 1000-qubit machines.",
  "content": "QpiAI has announced the development of India's most powerful quantum computer, code-named Indus Quantum Computer. This breakthrough achievement represents a significant step forward in India's quantum computing capabilities.\n\nThe company has revealed an ambitious roadmap for quantum computing development, with plans to scale up their technology significantly. Future iterations include the 64-qubit 'Kaveri' system, the 128-qubit 'Ganges' computer, and ultimately the 1000-qubit 'Everest' NISQ (Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum) quantum computer.\n\nThis development positions India among the select nations with advanced quantum computing capabilities, promising applications across various sectors including scientific research, cryptography, and complex computational problems.",
